{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity","id":1452419,"title":"Jedi in Trinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-15T23:05:06-07:00","id":1452419,"title":"Jedi in Trinity","content":"Well, not officially (please don't kill me Mr. Mouse), but honestly, this is one of the best new game systems I've had, and my players agree they'd prefer this over anything else for our new star wars rebels game.<br /> <br /> But how do we do jedi? Most classes, smugglers, etc, can be handled as Talents, especially wth the ability to &quot;I coincidentally grabbed the right tool to save myself&quot;.<br /> <br /> But Jedi have a lot of abilities, but not all of them are as dramatic as what psi's or novas get, so they're sort of a talent+some abilities. how would you kit them out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T23:44:49-07:00","id":1452422,"title":"","content":"Honestly I\u2019d just use Mesmerists for Jedi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T02:18:56-07:00","id":1452433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452422#post1452422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I\u2019d just use Mesmerists for Jedi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good answer.<br /> <br /> If you want to represent more precisely the jedi abilities, you could do your own list of gifts from talents, stalwarts and mesmerists. With such a list you could include mind tricks, combat prowess and whatever you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T03:19:35-07:00","id":1452438,"title":"","content":"You might need to scale up a bit. While not as powerful as a Nova, the Jedi are more powerful than Mesmerists. Think of Yoda lifting the spaceship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T03:53:39-07:00","id":1452440,"title":"","content":"Stalwarts have a Gift that lets them increase Scale in some ways. So make a variation of that and wham! You can keep them as Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T04:00:20-07:00","id":1452445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452438#post1452438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might need to scale up a bit. While not as powerful as a Nova, the Jedi are more powerful than Mesmerists. Think of Yoda lifting the spaceship.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could also build them as psiads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T05:35:50-07:00","id":1452452,"title":"","content":"I'd stick to mesmerists, and make Yoda an exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:47:42-07:00","id":1452495,"title":"","content":"I don't have the rules but From what I know maybe psiads would work well if you imposed limits on how high the characters could purchase psi and modes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:41:54-07:00","id":1452501,"title":"","content":"The problem of Psiads is they have a base se for powers linked to the powers they show, that Mesmerists don\u2019t have and so fit better in the Jedi concept.<br /> <br /> For example, any Psiad that have the Jedi mind trick would also be able to detect minds and project their thoughts in the target mind, what is not a common capacity to Jedi. But a Mesmerist has no basic set of powers (what is bad for them, but also good for the setting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:42:42-07:00","id":1452502,"title":"","content":"This is something that I have thought about a bit. I think that the solution that I would tend toward is the Psiad (with some restrictions on aptitudes/modes). However, I think that I would be inclined to also give the Jedi access to some Mesmerist/Stalwart/Talent gifts (basically from a predetermined list). Since the Psiad has the restrictions on the aptitudes/modes (no teleporting, limited biokinesis, probably no technokinesis, some restrictions on the psychokinesis, some other restrictions (and some dark side only restrictions (force lightning). I would be inclined to offer 1 mesmerist gift to start as well (not quite as strong as a full psiad), of course letting them spend Psi points to activate it.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that a &quot;Lightsaber&quot; could probably be built pretty well as bio-tech, like a Psi gauntlet but different shape. a little off flavor for some things but also helps explain why mainly Jedi use them (you could make it &quot;hard tech&quot; that requires formatting or something like that to fit the flavor better).<br /> <br /> Not to derail the thread but possibly to enhance the discussion:<br /> <br /> I have been curious why Novas and Psiads wouldn't have access to the Stalwart and Mesmerist gifts (that they would choose something else most of the time is another case entirely). Particularly in the case of Novas/Psiads that started out as Stalwarts/Mesmerists. For psions it could make sense for with the Prometheus chamber shenanigans. I think talents could always gain any talent/daredevil related gifts (thus expanding the core options with those in Adventure!).<br /> <br /> Is anyone planning to play a droid? are you making those as talents too, or low Quantum novas with limited options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:48:01-07:00","id":1452504,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> <br /> <br /> I agree and that makes sense. You could also &quot;replace&quot; certain powers from the modes (the ones that don't make sense) with Mesmerist powers that fit the general theme and traditional Jedi powers. I would personally like 1 per dot of the power (but just 1 flat may work better (not sure how they would balance)).<br /> <br /> Either way, psiad or Mesmerist, you can't really go wrong. I think that I like the Psiad flavor better personally, but it may take some work to get it just right.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T11:36:01-07:00","id":1452511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452452#post1452452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd stick to mesmerists, and make Yoda an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sound. But they'd have more inspiration points than a normal Mesmerist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T12:11:40-07:00","id":1452517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452504#post1452504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a><br /> <br /> I agree and that makes sense. You could also &quot;replace&quot; certain powers from the modes (the ones that don't make sense) with Mesmerist powers that fit the general theme and traditional Jedi powers. I would personally like 1 per dot of the power (but just 1 flat may work better (not sure how they would balance)).<br /> <br /> Either way, psiad or Mesmerist, you can't really go wrong. I think that I like the Psiad flavor better personally, but it may take some work to get it just right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on that. Psiads have a series of advantages that would fit great in the Jedi archetype, while Mesmerists would not fit on the frequency and power some Jedi use the force, but it\u2019s easier to fix the amount of inspiration than adapting the modes you need to reach that. Maybe you can make some gifts to make it cheaper to use gifts of certain aspects or increase the scale of a specific gift.<br /> <br /> Something to work on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T12:42:12-07:00","id":1452522,"title":"","content":"My response is to take the Stalwart and Mesmerist Gift tree and create a variant one from both that takes the skills one needs. This might mostly be Mesmerist yeah but there are some Stalwart stuff there as well, for example the paragon of humanity gift that gives scale. Its a bit of a time project but I totally could work. <br /> <br /> I also say keep Talents as is because in Star Wars talents are what people like Han Solo totally are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T15:12:13-07:00","id":1452544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452522#post1452522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My response is to take the Stalwart and Mesmerist Gift tree and create a variant one from both that takes the skills one needs. This might mostly be Mesmerist yeah but there are some Stalwart stuff there as well, for example the paragon of humanity gift that gives scale. Its a bit of a time project but I totally could work. <br /> <br /> I also say keep Talents as is because in Star Wars talents are what people like Han Solo totally are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking in first edition Adventure! speak, Han Solo is a Daredevil like Indiana Jones. ;-)<br /> <br /> In first edition Adventure! characters had 13 inspiration points. For Jedi I think 30 inspiration points sounds right to me. More powerful than normal Inspired PCs but only around the power level of the weakest Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T16:10:26-07:00","id":1452555,"title":"","content":"Didn't Obi-Wan sense the destruction of Alderaan from a significant distance? That sounds like a Psion/Psiad sensing a disaster within their Attunement range. If you look at Wookieepedia, there seem to be an absurdly large number of esoteric force powers in the extended Star Wars lore, many of which sound just like Psi powers: <a href=\"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Force_power/Legends\" target=\"_blank\">https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Force_power/Legends</a><br /> <br /> Looking through the various Aptitudes and their Modes, my first thoughts are:<br /> <br /> Biokinesis - Biosense sounds like a Force power, and the first few levels of Adaptation fit with the ability of some Jedi to control their own bodily processes. The other two Modes would either be unavailable or very rare disciplines.<br /> <br /> Clairsentience - Yep. They can do this.<br /> <br /> Electrokinesis - Most of these powers would either be unavailable or very rare disciplines, although Electromanipulation grants the power to detect living beings and lies/motivations without using the far more common (and readily countered) Telepathic powers, as well as granting the ability to hurl Force Lightning.<br /> <br /> Psychokinesis - Telekinesis is one of the most common Force abilities. The other two Modes would either be unavailable or very rare disciplines.<br /> <br /> Quantakinesis - The basic powers of Subquantum Sense and Psi Cloak sound very appropriate for Jedi and Sith respectively. The actual Modes would probably either be unavailable or very rare disciplines. I believe Psiads automatically get the basic powers even without putting dots into any of the Modes.<br /> <br /> Telepathy - Force users seem to make extensive use of many powers up through level 3, and masters dabble in the higher level stuff. Even the Network power sounds a lot like the Battle Meditation Force ability. Some few masters seem able to achieve Astral Life.<br /> <br /> Teleportation - The Spatial Sense basic power sounds like a Force power, but the effect is probably commonly achieved via a sensory power from another Aptitude. There is apparently a Force Travel power that lets you teleport, but using it corrupts you to the dark side.<br /> <br /> Vitakinesis - Yep. These powers should be okay for Force users.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> Looking further into the Wookieepedia article, Force Speed and Force Stealth are normally the first powers taught to Jedi. The first power would likely involve temporarily granting the Swift Edge via Biokinesis or Vitakinesis, while the second would be the Quantakinesis Psi Cloak power.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-16-2021, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T17:45:06-07:00","id":1452563,"title":"","content":"for me, Jedi are better seen in-lore as Psiads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T13:33:57-07:00","id":1453073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452563#post1452563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for me, Jedi are better seen in-lore as Psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div>I lean more Mesmerists, but that\u2019s a difference of where you want to set the dial on their powers vs the cinematic tropes facilitated by Dramatic Editing, rather than a difference in kind. Obvious different points in Star Wars media would be better represented by Psiads and other points by Mesmerists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T20:28:21-07:00","id":1453107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1452555#post1452555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Obi-Wan sense the destruction of Alderaan from a significant distance? That sounds like a Psion/Psiad sensing a disaster within their Attunement range. If you look at Wookieepedia, there seem to be an absurdly large number of esoteric force powers in the extended Star Wars lore, many of which sound just like Psi powers: <a href=\"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Force_power/Legends\" target=\"_blank\">https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Force_power/Legends</a><br /> <br /> Looking through the various Aptitudes and their Modes, my first thoughts are:<br /> <br /> Biokinesis - Biosense sounds like a Force power, and the first few levels of Adaptation fit with the ability of some Jedi to control their own bodily processes. The other two Modes would either be unavailable or very rare disciplines.<br /> <br /> Clairsentience - Yep. They can do this.<br /> <br /> Electrokinesis - Most of these powers would either be unavailable or very rare disciplines, although Electromanipulation grants the power to detect living beings and lies/motivations without using the far more common (and readily countered) Telepathic powers, as well as granting the ability to hurl Force Lightning.<br /> <br /> Psychokinesis - Telekinesis is one of the most common Force abilities. The other two Modes would either be unavailable or very rare disciplines.<br /> <br /> Quantakinesis - The basic powers of Subquantum Sense and Psi Cloak sound very appropriate for Jedi and Sith respectively. The actual Modes would probably either be unavailable or very rare disciplines. I believe Psiads automatically get the basic powers even without putting dots into any of the Modes.<br /> <br /> Telepathy - Force users seem to make extensive use of many powers up through level 3, and masters dabble in the higher level stuff. Even the Network power sounds a lot like the Battle Meditation Force ability. Some few masters seem able to achieve Astral Life.<br /> <br /> Teleportation - The Spatial Sense basic power sounds like a Force power, but the effect is probably commonly achieved via a sensory power from another Aptitude. There is apparently a Force Travel power that lets you teleport, but using it corrupts you to the dark side.<br /> <br /> Vitakinesis - Yep. These powers should be okay for Force users.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> Looking further into the Wookieepedia article, Force Speed and Force Stealth are normally the first powers taught to Jedi. The first power would likely involve temporarily granting the Swift Edge via Biokinesis or Vitakinesis, while the second would be the Quantakinesis Psi Cloak power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how Blasters are defined, Vader absorbing the bolts that Han Solo fired at him in Empire is some version of Electrokinesis, Theromkinesis or Quantakinesis. Meanwhile advanced Latrosis healing technique should be disallowed for the most part. Apparently Rey Palpatine/Skywalker was the first Jedi to use those abilities and that was in The Rise of Skywalker. There's a reason Luke had to get a cybernetic hand and Vader had to get cybernetic almost everything. The Force didn't let them just grow stuff back. I think it's also best to assume that pretty much anything involving Teleportation of &quot;right out.&quot;<br /> <br /> One other thing to consider is that Jedi/Sith never really seemed to get tired or &quot;run out of Force Mana&quot; or anything like that. The thing that keeps Jedi in line is concern about falling to the Dark Side. You might consider bringing in some version of &quot;Transcendence&quot; and &quot;Quantum Flux&quot; to represent &quot;dark side points.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T10:53:18-07:00","id":1453183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1452419-jedi-in-trinity?p=1453107#post1453107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile advanced Latrosis healing technique should be disallowed for the most part. Apparently Rey Palpatine/Skywalker was the first Jedi to use those abilities and that was in The Rise of Skywalker. There's a reason Luke had to get a cybernetic hand and Vader had to get cybernetic almost everything. The Force didn't let them just grow stuff back.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Wookieepedia, Force Healing was quite common: <a href=\"https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Force_healing/Legends\" target=\"_blank\">https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Force_healing/Legends</a><br /> The wiki claims it made its first appearance in the first Star Wars movie, when Obi-Wan healed Luke on Tatooine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-22-2021, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T11:28:58-07:00","id":1453186,"title":"","content":"I choose the whole Gift structure of the Mesmerist/Stalwart because I like the idea of the individually purchased power system for the Jedi. Having there be a variant of the nova Max Out rules could totally provide a basis for when a Jedi does something somewhat arbitrarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T17:58:42-07:00","id":1453219,"title":"","content":"Note that the upcoming TC:A! will be giving stalwarts a \u201cmax out\u201d Dramatic Editing variant, and mesmerists will be getting an \u201cimprovise some other power\u201d DE variant. Personally, I would have given <i>both</i> of those to Stalwarts (and to novas, for that matter; comic books are jam-packed with the same plot convenience issues that DE represents, and not just for the likes of Batman), and I would have given mesmerists something about attunement and cooperative power use. Maybe allow all three types of Inspired to access all three kinds of Dramatic Editing, but with each getting a discount in one type and a price inflation in the other two. <br /> <br /> But with regard to Force users? I'd go with them being a balance: all three kinds of Dramatic Editing available at the normal cost: no discounts, no surcharges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T09:40:09-07:00","id":1453460,"title":"","content":"my 2 cents: use Mesmerists, 3 kinds of Gifts: Neutral Gifts, Lightside Gifts, Darkside Gifts (XP cost and cost to use based on current character behavior). Probably change &quot;Gift&quot; to &quot;Technique&quot; for better coupling of systems and lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T09:48:43-07:00","id":1453462,"title":"","content":"In terms of the selection of Gifts, I agree: there may be the occasional Dynamic or Heroic Gift in the mix; but the bulk of them should be Psychic. <br /> <br /> And yeah, you might want to introduce a system representing the Light Side / Dark Side dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":